# Architecture (fit)

- Keep domain logic independent from Next.js and Expo concerns.
- UI and route handlers in `app/` orchestrate data flow; heavy business rules belong in `lib/`.
- Shared utilities in `lib/` should stay framework-agnostic when possible.
- Isolate side effects (network, storage, Capacitor/native APIs) behind thin adapters.

## Do

- Prefer dependency injection or thin adapters at boundaries.
- When changing data flow, note Client vs Server component boundaries and state implications.

## Don't

- Couple reusable business rules to component lifecycle or App Router behavior.
